<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>At least one and exactly one for independent events</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>[[if test="is(cx=0)"]]Otieno buys two solar lamps from different suppliers. The probability that the first lamp still works after a year is \({@pdec(p)@}\), and for the second lamp it is \({@pdec(q)@}\).[[elif test="is(cx=1)"]]Two boda boda riders are stopped at a checkpoint. The probability that the first rider has a valid licence is \({@pdec(p)@}\), and for the second rider it is \({@pdec(q)@}\).[[else]]Chebet buys two passion-fruit seedlings from different nurseries. The probability that the first seedling survives is \({@pdec(p)@}\), and for the second it is \({@pdec(q)@}\).[[/if]] These events are independent.</p><p>Give each probability exactly, as a fraction or an exact decimal.</p><p>(a) Find the probability that both [[if test="is(cx=0)"]]lamps work[[elif test="is(cx=1)"]]riders have a valid licence[[else]]seedlings survive[[/if]].</p><div>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Find the probability that [[if test="is(cx=0)"]]neither lamp works[[elif test="is(cx=1)"]]neither rider has a valid licence[[else]]neither seedling survives[[/if]].</p><div>[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) Find the probability that [[if test="is(cx=0)"]]at least one lamp works[[elif test="is(cx=1)"]]at least one rider has a valid licence[[else]]at least one seedling survives[[/if]].</p><div>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div><p>(d) Find the probability that [[if test="is(cx=0)"]]exactly one lamp works[[elif test="is(cx=1)"]]exactly one rider has a valid licence[[else]]exactly one seedling survives[[/if]].</p><div>[[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) Both: \({@pdec(p)@} \times {@pdec(q)@} = {@pdec(ta1)@}\).</p><p>(b) Neither: \((1 - {@pdec(p)@}) \times (1 - {@pdec(q)@}) = {@pdec(1-p)@} \times {@pdec(1-q)@} = {@pdec(ta2)@}\).</p><p>(c) <q>At least one</q> is everything except <q>neither</q>: \(1 - {@pdec(ta2)@} = {@pdec(ta3)@}\).</p><p>(d) Exactly one is the first only or the second only: \({@pdec(p)@} \times {@pdec(1-q)@} + {@pdec(1-p)@} \times {@pdec(q)@} = {@pdec(p*(1-q))@} + {@pdec((1-p)*q)@} = {@pdec(ta4)@}\). Check: both, exactly one and neither add to \({@pdec(ta1)@} + {@pdec(ta4)@} + {@pdec(ta2)@} = 1\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
