  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Probability III: at least one and exactly one for independent events</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Essential 3.2: Find P(both), P(neither), P(at least one) by the complement and P(exactly one) for two independent events.</p><p id="edition">Essential</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Chapter 3, Exercise D, question 2 of Cassell, D., Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P. and Shilton, S., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Statistics 1 for Edexcel, Cambridge University Press, 2004: four parts (both, neither, at least one, exactly one) with new Kenyan contexts and new numbers, randomised.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Essential Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
